.TH tunl 1 0.29.0 tclutils "Tcl Utility Command"
.SH NAME
tunl \- thin CLI wrapper for tclutils::tunl
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
tunl ?-style all|nonempty|none? ?-start N? ?-increment N? ?-width N? ?-separator S? ?file?
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The tunl command is a thin wrapper around the Tcl package tclutils::tunl. It is intended for interactive and scripting use when tclutils is installed from source. The primary API remains the Tcl library; see tunl(n) for procedures, options, and semantics.
.PP
Run the script with tclsh:
.PP
.nf
tclsh bin/tunl.tcl ...
.fi
